<h1>Getting Started</h1>

<h2>Install the extension</h2>

<p>From the project root, in order:</p>

<ol>
  <li>Install dependencies once: <code>npm install</code></li>
  <li>Build + package: <code>npm run package</code>. This cleans any old <code>hyperdoc-*.vsix</code>, builds the bundle, and writes a fresh <code>hyperdoc-&lt;version&gt;.vsix</code> — so only the current version's file is ever left in the root.</li>
  <li>Install into your main VS Code — the <code>.vsix</code> filename carries the version from <code>package.json</code>, so let the shell fill it in rather than hardcoding it: <code>code --install-extension "hyperdoc-$((Get-Content package.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json).version).vsix" --force</code></li>
  <li>Reload <strong>every already-open VS Code window</strong>: <strong>Ctrl+Shift+P</strong> → "Developer: Reload Window" (or restart VS Code). Installing a VSIX does not update windows that are already running — this is the most common reason a rebuild still shows the old editor.</li>
</ol>

<p>For ongoing iteration the build / package / install steps can be chained (PowerShell):</p>

<pre><code>npm run package; code --install-extension "hyperdoc-$((Get-Content package.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json).version).vsix" --force</code></pre>

<h2>Create your first .hd file</h2>

<p>Create any file with a <code>.hd</code> extension in a workspace. VS Code launches the HD WYSIWYG editor as the default editor for that file. On first open, the editor injects an <code>id</code> and a <code>version</code> into the frontmatter — you don't need to set them by hand.</p>

<p>If you want to seed your own frontmatter, start the file with a bare YAML fence:</p>

<pre><code>---
title: My Document
description: A short description.
---

&lt;h1&gt;Hello, HD&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;…&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>

<h2>Editor basics</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Toolbar</strong> at the top: headings, bold/italic/underline, inline code, code block, links, lists, blockquote, horizontal rule, insert table. The toolbar stays fixed in place as you scroll, so it's always reachable.</li>
  <li><strong>Keyboard shortcuts</strong>: <strong>Ctrl+B</strong>/<strong>I</strong>/<strong>U</strong> for bold/italic/underline, <strong>Ctrl+K</strong> for link (insert if text is selected, edit if cursor is inside an existing link), <strong>Ctrl+Alt+1</strong>…<strong>6</strong> for headings, <strong>Ctrl+E</strong> for inline code. Full table in <a href="editor.hd">Editor Features</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Tables</strong>: hover near the top to insert columns, near the left to insert rows. Right-click any cell for the full menu (delete column/row, toggle headers, delete table). Hover a column boundary to resize.</li>
  <li><strong>Paste from Markdown</strong>: paste Markdown text — the editor detects it and converts automatically.</li>
  <li><strong>Paste from HTML</strong>: paste HTML from Notion, Linear, or browsers — the editor sanitizes against the HD allow-list.</li>
  <li><strong>Copy as Markdown</strong>: <strong>Ctrl+Shift+P</strong> → "HD: Copy as Markdown".</li>
</ul>

